{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1060617-resisted-endowments","id":1060617,"title":"resisted endowments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-09T12:54:23-08:00","id":1060617,"title":"resisted endowments","content":"Current group is working on a custom endowment. The core hunter book has design questions you are supposed to ask (can it be resisted), but i guess my question is when in your opinion should an endowment be resisted/contested? One player suggested anytime a power tries to take control of a person/creature (mind or body) it should be resisted. What process do you all use? This will mainly involve benedictions/holy gifts and powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12209-adonus","name":"adonus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T22:58:20-08:00","id":1061143,"title":"","content":"Powers that have a potent or overwhelming binary effect (either it works or it doesn't) should incline towards being contested.<br /> Powers that have a sliding scale of effect, where the number of rolled successes matters to the magnitude of the result, or powers that have a binary effect that doesn't overwhelm the target and thus generally are more interesting when they succeed more often than not, should incline towards being resisted.<br /> <br /> Salt to taste.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T04:13:08-08:00","id":1061194,"title":"","content":"As above. Control powers are usually contested, roll vs roll. As far as I know, the type of endowment is not a factor, but I appreciate the attempt to give as much info as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}